      "id": "S2",
      "synthetic": true,
      "label": "Fabricated teaching excerpt 2",
      "identifier": { "type": "url", "value": "https://example.org/teaching-study-2" },
      "sourceExcerpt": "A computer-generated sequence assigned 60 participants equally. Allocation concealment was not described. Outcome assessors were blinded. At 8 weeks the mean difference was 1.2 points (95% CI -0.5 to 2.9). Attrition was 12/60 without reasons.",
      "design": "randomized-controlled-trial",
      "designNote": "Assignment used a computer-generated sequence, which is an unpredictable allocation mechanism; the design is taken from this method and not from what the excerpt calls it.",
      "instrument": null,
      "instrumentNote": "No appraisal instrument was applied to this excerpt; the ratings below are the platform's own structured judgement and are not a Rob 2, ROBINS-I or GRADE certification.",
      "domains": {
        "riskOfBias": {
          "rating": "serious",
          "reason": "Two steps. Attrition: 12/60 participants did not complete and the excerpt gives no reasons ('Attrition was 12/60 without reasons'), so differential or informative dropout cannot be excluded. Reporting: allocation concealment was not described and no analysis population is stated, so whether allocation was concealed and how the 12 non-completers were handled cannot be checked."
        },
        "indirectness": {
          "rating": "serious",
          "reason": "The excerpt gives no population information, so the distance from an adult population cannot be assessed, and the outcome is a 1.2-point mean difference on an unnamed scale ('points') with no minimal important difference, so its clinical relevance is undefined. The 8-week time point does match the question."
        },
        "imprecision": {
          "rating": "serious",
          "reason": "The reported interval is 95% CI -0.5 to 2.9 on an unnamed scale. It crosses no difference and extends from a small worsening to a difference several times the point estimate, so it spans both a worthwhile and a non-worthwhile effect and does not support a decision."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "bodies": [
    {
      "outcomeId": "O1",
      "outcome": "Improvement at 8-week follow-up",
      "studyIds": ["S1", "S2"],
      "startingCertainty": "high",
      "startingCertaintyReason": "The body contains an interventional randomized trial (S2); starting certainty follows the design of the body, and the shortfall of the set is taken as a named downgrade below rather than as a lower starting rung.",
      "downgrades": [
        {
          "domain": "riskOfBias",
          "steps": 2,
          "reason": "S1: alternating allocation and unblinded outcome assessors, with no prespecified protocol. S2: 12/60 participants lost without reasons, allocation concealment not described. Both studies carry serious risk-of-bias findings in the domains each was rated on, and neither reports a protocol or registration to check against."
        },
        {
          "domain": "indirectness",
          "steps": 1,
          "reason": "Neither excerpt states the population, so the body does not establish applicability to an adult population, and neither defines the improvement measure or a minimal important difference for the outcome being asked about."
        },
        {
          "domain": "inconsistency",
          "steps": 1,
          "reason": "The two studies do not point the same way and their effect measures are not commensurable: S1 reports counts ('24/40 versus 20/40 participants improved') on a dichotomous improvement outcome without an interval, and S2 reports a mean difference of 1.2 points (95% CI -0.5 to 2.9) whose interval includes no difference. With two studies, an unexplained divergence in direction and in outcome scale cannot be resolved."
        },
        {
          "domain": "imprecision",
          "steps": 2,
          "reason": "S2's interval (95% CI -0.5 to 2.9) crosses no difference and spans a small worsening to a large benefit on an undefined scale, and S1 reports no interval at all. Neither study supplies an estimate precise enough to act on."
        },
        {
          "domain": "publicationBias",
          "steps": 0,
          "reason": "Considered and not acted on. S1 states that no prespecified protocol was provided and neither excerpt reports registration, so reporting completeness could not be checked; with a set of two, funnel-plot or small-study analysis is not interpretable and no step was taken for it."
        }
      ],
      "upgrades": [],
      "certainty": "very-low",
      "certaintyArithmetic": "high (4) - riskOfBias 2 - indirectness 1 - inconsistency 1 - imprecision 2 + 0 = below the floor of 1, so very-low",
      "whatWouldChange": "A protocol or registration record for either study; an analysis population statement accounting for the 12 non-completers in S2; an interval for S1's improvement comparison; the population definition, age range and recruitment setting for both studies; and the definition of the improvement outcome with its minimal important difference. A further study reporting the same 8-week outcome in an adult population on a common scale would allow the direction of the two excerpts to be compared rather than merely noted as divergent."
    }
  ]
}

